    if (callNow) {
      func.apply(this, args);
    }
  };
}
```

## How It Works

| Concept | Description |
|---|---|
| **Closure** | `timeoutId` is trapped in the closure of `debounced`, persisting across calls. |
| **Trailing edge** (default) | The function only executes *after* `wait` ms of inactivity. |
| **Leading edge** (`immediate = true`) | The function executes *immediately* on the first call, then suppresses subsequent calls during the debounce period. |
| **`this` context** | `func.apply(this, args)` preserves the original `this` binding. |
| **`...args`** | Captures and forwards all arguments from the debounced call. |

